<!doctype html><html lang="zh-CN"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Current1390 score-map precision boundary</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#101a29;color:#e7edf7;font:16px/1.8 "Microsoft YaHei",sans-serif}main{max-width:1150px;margin:auto;padding:24px}a{color:#9fd5ff}nav{position:sticky;top:0;background:#172638;padding:12px;z-index:2;display:flex;gap:22px;flex-wrap:wrap}pre{overflow:auto;background:#09131f;padding:16px}code{font:13px/1.7 Consolas,monospace}table{border-collapse:collapse;display:block;overflow:auto}td,th{border:1px solid #45617e;padding:8px 12px}blockquote{border-left:4px solid #e7b667;margin:18px 0;padding:1px 16px;background:#203249}h1,h2,h3,h4{scroll-margin-top:85px}img{max-width:100%}.meta{font-size:12px;color:#a9bfd3;overflow-wrap:anywhere}summary{cursor:pointer}</style><nav><a href="../../../framework-architecture.html">主架构</a><a href="../../main-ui-map.html">逆向核心</a><a href="../index.html">关联文档目录</a><a data-source-download download href="../../../plugins/GRAY-MATCH-SCORE-MAP-PRECISION-SOURCE.md">下载原始文件</a></nav><main><h1 id="current1390-score-map-precision-boundary">Current1390 score-map precision boundary</h1><p>Same-hash core <code>MVD_Algorithm.dll</code> SHA85D17ECC87D52E9A62D8BB86C8D5208AC999BCD31EC6D0806453F8165733F549. Private read-only Ghidra explicit instruction spans: <code>analysis/gray-match/core-boundary/output/180c92930-explicit-span.asm.txt</code> and <code>180c93310-explicit-span.asm.txt</code>. The small .pdata runtime fragment sizes are not complete body coverage; these are explicitly bounded decoded spans, not a claim that all blocks or callees are recovered.</p>
<p>The actual normalization result is not kept as double throughout candidate production. At <code>180c92d2d</code> the selected dot callback <code>[RSI+120]</code> executes. The value at stack+c8 is loaded as double, added to stack+80 by ADDSD at d52, and sent with the other original double operands to <code>180c9ad00</code> at d61. Return XMM0 is converted <strong>CVTSD2SS at d79</strong>, then stored into the score-map float cell at d89. The following branch compares the original <strong>double XMM0</strong> against a float threshold promoted by CVTSS2SD from <code>[RSI+118]</code> at d8e. Therefore substituting the rounded map float for that immediate double threshold comparison is not justified.</p>
<p>Candidate scan <code>180c937ae</code> reloads a score-map <strong>float</strong>. COMISS against XMM14 followed by JA takes a separate block at9390c (outside the current explicit span); COMISS against XMM13 followed by JBE skips insertion. The shown insertion path executes <strong>SQRTSS at937c4</strong>, then calls <code>180c97e60</code> at937f2 with XMM3 carrying that single-precision square root. Neither double sqrt nor sqrt-before-map-rounding is source-equivalent to this path. Upper branch9390c and register threshold definitions remain exact local continuation gaps; do not generalize the shown path to all peaks.</p>
<p>Production scalar normalization currently has strict12 original-bit checks; map storage and candidate scanner are not implemented by those checks. Full1390 training/search, layout and remaining candidate/refinement paths remain incomplete. This evidence narrows the required next implementation boundary without adding real-image samples or guessing scoring rules.</p>
